WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.250
Good morning John, it’s question
Tuesday, the day that I answer

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.210
real questions from real
Nerdfighters.

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.210
And it’s not really

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.430
Tuesday, and it’s not really
going to be me.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:08.430
Like the

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.900
Nerdfighters are real, the questions
are real, but am I real?

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.850
Shuffle is a podcast app, and
yes in thanks for doing this

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.680
I do have to say you should
check out their service, I

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.280
actually think it’d be pretty
cool if a lot of Nerdfighters

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.760
used it for Dear Hank &amp; John
because you get to like

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.779
react and interact with the
podcast with other people

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:22.779
kind of.

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:24.080
So that might be cool.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.460
But regardless, the point is

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.160
they have taken the tremendous
amount of transcripts of the

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.880
world you and I have said, John.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.530
And they have created an AI

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.360
chat bot that is a mash up of
the two of us.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.360
Which is something

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.710
else because sometimes you
can tell when it’s you and when it’s me.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.620
And so I am doing a Question
Tuesday, but I’m not answering

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.920
the questions.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.399
Artificial Hank
and John are.

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:46.460
Rachel asks,

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.650
what should I do about the
creeping dread?

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:52.680
Hmm… I would recommend that you try to do
the thing that you need to do to

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.780
reach those goals. Then turn
that into excitement because you’re

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.150
about to go for it.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.340
I mean that
one was me.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.340
That one’s definitely me.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.009
It sounds like
good advice. Is it? Probably not.

00:01:04.009 --> 00:01:05.340
Most of the stuff that
sounds like good advice isn’t.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.259
Megan wants to know, do
you play minecraft?

00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:10.539
Minecraft minecraft minecraft
minecraft minecraft.

00:01:10.539 --> 00:01:11.789
How many socks are too
many socks?

00:01:11.789 --> 00:01:13.109
I don’t know, 12.

00:01:13.109 --> 00:01:16.030
This of all the things the
AI said I think is the most inaccurate.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:18.500
I own a sock subscription
for charity, there’s no such thing

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.500
as too many socks.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.200
You’re
challenged to a duel, what’s the

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.200
weapon?

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.435
Trampoline dodge ball. I mean, hell yeah.

00:01:24.435 --> 00:01:25.115
That, yes.

00:01:25.115 --> 00:01:26.606
Oat Milk Stan wants to know,

00:01:26.606 --> 00:01:27.743
what do you recommend to
pass the time while I recover

00:01:27.743 --> 00:01:28.743
from wisdom teeth removal?

00:01:28.743 --> 00:01:30.669
I would recommend that if you

00:01:30.669 --> 00:01:33.130
have wisdom teeth removed
recently, that watching Crash

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.299
Course videos at twice speed is
probably the best way to pass

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:37.299
the time.

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:38.299
Is it?

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:39.299
Like just after
anesthesia?

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:40.299
Did you mean half speed?

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:43.372
Chicken fingers dipped in applesauce
or French fries dipped in Frosty?

00:01:43.372 --> 00:01:45.822
Definitely French fries dipped in
something because in something because

00:01:46.599 --> 00:01:50.130
in any comparative tasting of applesauce or
French fries dipped in Frosty, the

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.469
French fries are going to win
every time.

00:01:52.469 --> 00:01:53.739
I mean with a very tiny

00:01:53.739 --> 00:01:57.509
exception that sounds like
exactly what I would say.

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:00.270
Is there a specific reason humans
get so attached to stuffed animals?

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.649
I think it’s natural selection.

00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:03.809
I think that as we’ve evolved to be more

00:02:03.809 --> 00:02:06.939
social we’ve sort of developed
the need for that attachment

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:11.180
through activities like filmmaking,
music, art-- still forms of

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.519
storytelling-- or you can tell a story.

00:02:13.519 --> 00:02:14.860
We got a little lost at the end there

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.410
but that is a vlogbrothers vibe.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.090
When eating a bicycle, where should one start?

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.870
I would venture to say
the handlebars first.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.760
The spokes  might try to escape or rebel, and the
tire could explode.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:26.760
That there feels very

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:27.900
uncanny valley to me.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.730
It’s like it
thinks it knows what it’s like to be a

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.400
person but it actually doesn’t.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:32.540
If you could turn one person into a

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.129
pelican who would it be and why?

00:02:34.129 --> 00:02:36.549
I’d like to turn Prince Harry into a pelican

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:37.989
because he can dance like one.

00:02:37.989 --> 00:02:39.270
I mean that’s funnier than anything I

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.420
would have said.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.349
That’s funnier than
anything I would have said.

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:45.079
Favorite cursed item Nerdfighteria has
turned into a meme?

00:02:45.079 --> 00:02:48.140
Oh god, I don’t know that we’ve
cursed any specific item.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.770
We discovered the train song huh huh and we didn’t
realize that that was cursed, but it’s cursed.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.520
I don’t know for sure what train
song the AI is talking about here,

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:56.890
but I’m pretty sure it’s this one.

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:00.849
All aboard the choo choo train, all aboard all aboard.

00:03:00.849 --> 00:03:01.849
Did I discover that?

00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:05.060
No. I kinda
rediscovered it though, and I like it

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.370
and it is also cursed.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.930
Favorite social media platform?

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.640
I like Twitter a lot because I get
there first thing in the morning

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.530
and they blur the lines a bit between
what’s news and what’s not news.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:19.730
That actually made me
feel a little bit too seen, AI bot.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:20.730
Best pizza topping?

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.670
Not a day has gone by
when I haven’t thought wistfully of the

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:28.510
pepperocinis and mushroom pizzas
I used to eat while I lived in Ohio.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:33.200
It remains in my brain as the perfect
marriage of pepperoni and fungus.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.750
And that’s some hardcore
John Green vibes for you right there.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:38.159
And let’s finish off with one from
Payton who asks, what is

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:39.450
your new furby’s name?

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:42.620
It’s not named yet, so the AI gets to do
it.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:43.620
It’s Philip.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.959
This has been delightful,
if a little unsettling.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:48.380
I was having kind of a hard time
 figuring out how to end this video.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:51.760
But then I realized I could just turn to the AI.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.980
John, wear sunscreen.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.780
I’ll see you on Tuesday.

